DELIVERABLE — parity port of web features/admin/components/devtools/ReferenceLinksSection.tsx (+ constants.ts)
  feature-views/ReferenceLinksSection.cs           WinUI 3 view. Responsive 1/2/4-column card grid mirroring
        the web `grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4`. Each card = TsGlassPanel (the @/components/ui GlassPanel
        equivalent) wrapping a HyperlinkButton whose NavigateUri opens the destination in the system browser
        (the native <a target=_blank rel=noopener> equivalent), with a cyan accent icon tile (token-tinted),
        the localized title, and the verbatim URL caption. Renders Ready (grid) and Empty (friendly state,
        never a blank box). Narrator name on the root landmark and on every link; no custom animation so the
        system reduced-motion preference is honoured; font sizes scale with the system text-scaling setting.
  feature-views/ReferenceLinksSection.Model.cs     WinUI-free. Static catalog (4 links; URLs byte-for-byte and
        i18n keys verbatim from the web constant), ReferenceLinkIcon -> Segoe Fluent glyph map, localized
        projection, registration (Slug="ReferenceLinksSection"), PII-safe diagnostics (view.opened slug=...).
  feature-views/ReferenceLinksSection.ViewModel.cs WinUI-free P1/S8 state holder (INotifyPropertyChanged):
        Ready/Empty state, Items projection, RegionName/EmptyMessage, Reload() re-resolves labels on language
        change (react-i18next parity). No HTTP (the web surface has none).
  TeslaSync.App.Tests/FeatureViews/ReferenceLinksSectionTests.cs   14 headless tests: catalog parity (verbatim
        URLs + keys), projection adapter, EXACT i18n key requests, glyph map, Ready/Empty branches, a11y
        AutomationName + region label, Reload re-projection, registration slug, diagnostics. All PASS.

STATES — faithful to the web source (no fabricated async states)
  The web ReferenceLinksSection consumes NO asynchronous data: it binds only useTranslation and maps the
  static REFERENCE_LINKS constant. It therefore has no fetch/loading/error/stale/offline branches. The honest
  native reproduction is Ready (the populated grid) plus a defensive Empty surface. Inventing async
  loading/error/offline/stale states the source does not have would be silent drift; they are intentionally
  and transparently omitted (and this is documented here rather than papered over).

i18n
  4 web title keys reproduced verbatim: devtools.ref.fleetOverview / partnerEndpoints / devPortal /
  telemetryGuide. 2 accessibility keys added: devtools.ref.regionLabel, devtools.ref.empty. All 6 resolve via
  the ILocalizer facade with English fallbacks AND are registered in apps/windows/Strings/en/Resources.resw as
  translation.devtools.ref.* . NB: these keys are anonymous even in the web catalog (web/src/i18n/en.json has
  no devtools.ref.* entries), so the English fallbacks here ARE the canonical copy.

